02:11 HaSHEM thunders his voice before his army; For his forces are very great; For he is strong who obeys his command; For the day of HaSHEM is great and very awesome, And who can endure it?
02:12 "Yet even now," says HaSHEM, "turn to me with all your heart, And with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning."
02:13 Tear your heart, and not your garments, And turn to HaSHEM, your G-D; For he is gracious and merciful, Slow to anger, and abundant in lovingkindness, And relents from sending calamity.
02:14 Who knows? He may turn and relent, And leave a blessing behind him, Even a meal offering and a drink offering to HaSHEM, your G-D.
02:15 Blow the shofar in Tzion! Sanctify a fast. Call a solemn assembly.
02:16 Gather the people. Sanctify the assembly. Assemble the Zakenim. Gather the children, and those who suck the breasts. Let the bridegroom go forth from his room, And the bride out of her chamber.
02:17 Let the Cohanim, the ministers of HaSHEM, weep between the porch and the altar, And let them say, "Spare your people, HaSHEM, And don't give your heritage to reproach, That the nations should rule over them. Why should they say among the peoples, 'Where is their G-D?'"2:18 Then HaSHEM was jealous for his land, And had pity on his people.2:19 HaSHEM answered his people, "Behold, I will send you grain, new wine, and oil, And you will be satisfied with them; And I will no more make you a reproach among the nations.
02:18 Then HaSHEM was jealous for his land, And had pity on his people.
02:19 HaSHEM answered his people, "Behold, I will send you grain, new wine, and oil, And you will be satisfied with them; And I will no more make you a reproach among the nations.
02:20 But I will remove the northern army far away from you, And will drive it into a barren and desolate land, Its front into the eastern sea, And its back into the western sea; And its stench will come up, And its bad smell will rise." Surely he has done great things.
02:21 Land, don't be afraid. Be glad and rejoice, for HaSHEM has done great things.
02:22 Don't be afraid, you animals of the field; For the pastures of the wilderness spring up, For the tree bears its fruit. The fig tree and the vine yield their strength.
02:23 "Be glad then, you children of Tzion, And rejoice in HaSHEM, your G-D; For he gives you the former rain in just measure, And he causes the rain to come down for you, The former rain and the latter rain, As before.
02:24 The threshing floors will be full of wheat, And the vats will overflow with new wine and oil.
02:25 I will restore to you the years that the swarming locust has eaten, The great locust, the grasshopper, and the caterpillar, My great army, which I sent among you.
02:26 You will have plenty to eat, and be satisfied, And will praise the name of HaSHEM, your G-D, Who has dealt wondrously with you; And my people will never again be put to shame.
02:27 You will know that I am in the midst of Yisra'el, And that I am HaSHEM, your G-D, and there is no one else; And my people will never again be put to shame.
